WEBVTT

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.860
Fifteen fatalities.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.230
They progress to the same point as Dewanosuke.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.570
Two cases of insanity.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.700
The research is going well too.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.540
Blade of the Immortal

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.960
One, two, three

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.260
Undead tree

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.680
What truth

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:58.350
I'll come true

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.060
Wow, wow, wow, wow

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.400
And I see that bright light

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.360
This is all I have

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.950
What did you say?
I know

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.830
Why do you say?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.500
Hone the blade lie around

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:37.550
Survive of vision
Death and pleasure are my future

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.720
I got lost
I was lost

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:45.310
Survive of vision

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:48.730
Unfinished heaven

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.570
Now fight to claim your wounds

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:56.610
Don't know why
Don't know why

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.910
Survive of vision

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.420
What's your name?

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.550
Kuichiru.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.010
You?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.520
Feniche Isaac Calvario.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.060
I can only remember the "Isaku" part.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.270
Then "Isaku" is fine.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.580
Isaku, give me an adult name.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.870
We have to live strong together.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.670
You can't be calling me "Kuichiru"
like I'm some kid.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:58.010
-Then how about "Toa"?
-What's that?

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:01.930
I guess it's fine. So it's Isaku and Toa now.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.520
Hey.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.480
I'm going to the jail in Kodemacho. Want to come?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.650
What's that?

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.690
The place where people arrested
by the government are taken.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.230
Where is it?

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.400
I'll say this now.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.780
We're not going there to kill people.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.830
-Well, can you see?
-Isaku's not there.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.540
Well, it's not like we'd see him right away.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:37.500
But if Mr. Isaku is here, you should look closely
at which building he's in.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.510
We'll figure something out.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.510
As long as you can manage to stay calm.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.600
FOUR DAYS LATER

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.020
Isaku still isn't here!

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.690
Yelling at me won't help.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.190
But this certainly is strange.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.610
Mr. Isaku aside, where is everyone else?

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.120
Rin. I need to make a stop somewhere.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.330
I'm going to ask an old guy I know for advice.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.250
What? Wait, hold on!

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.520
Isaku. Change into this.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.440
You'll stand out too much in that.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.820
Kuichiru.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.610
Is this the journey you were talking about?

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.110
It's not Kuichiru, it's Toa.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.860
This is just a one-time thing.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.990
Besides, these people stole lots of stuff
from the Ainu.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.080
I'm just taking it back.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.540
Let's head to the sea.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.750
I want to go somewhere where no one knows me.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.130
-There they are!
-Over there!

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.640
Toa, you dummy! What have you done?

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.980
Stealing is one thing, but killing?

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.440
But I was starving. I had no choice.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.610
They pointed their guns at me
for trying to take some jerky.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.740
Everything got so confusing. I just...

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.630
This isn't the mountains, Isaku.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.010
Even with good manners, you'll still be robbed.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:56.480
Toa, if we head further south from here,
I think we really will find it.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.310
A mountain that no one else owns.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.190
Then, let's build a house at the foot of it.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:05.530
There, let's make a living,
growing potatoes and such.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.870
Potatoes do sound fun.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.750
Isaku.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.460
Don't abandon me.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.330
Don't disappear, okay?

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.920
That won't happen.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.550
Before I left on this journey, my father told me

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.050
I'm not cut out to be the son of a priest,

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:35.270
but the fact that you appeared before me
may have been a sign from God.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:42.980
A sign to live on and walk by Toa's side,
guiding her.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:48.740
Go on, Sakutaro.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.070
Tell your father.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.700
You were to train the boy, starting today.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.910
Oh, that's right.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:58.160
Apologies, Sakutaro.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.710
If your father had just a little more time...

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.920
It gives me great pride
to have such a busy father.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.010
That's Kagimura Habaki.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.550
And there's Mrs. Habaki.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.140
And their son.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.940
Monitor Kagimura Habaki.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.730
As soon as he takes any action outside his duties,

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.030
he should be going to where Manji is.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.530
Oops...

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.910
Look, it's him.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.240
So that's...

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.660
Such an ill temper upon his face.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.620
Immortality experiments in the dungeon.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.880
-The absurdity.
-That's the devil's handiwork.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:26.250
Doa?

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.800
Thank goodness.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.220
I was getting worried because you never came back.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.220
Hey--

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.560
-Immortality experiments?
-Yeah.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.810
So you were able to hear what they said,

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:47.110
but there were too many constables
and you couldn't get home?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.270
Yeah.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.490
Your body is small and you're quick.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.070
I'm sure you could've avoided them if you tried.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:56.820
If I were with Isaku,

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.530
killing the whole lot of them would've been easy.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.700
But now,

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.500
without Isaku, I'm...

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.880
I don't know what to do on my own.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.810
-They're really in a place like this?
-Yeah.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:24.980
They didn't say explicitly,
but it matches what the householder maps say.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:27.400
Are those maps of Edo Castle really--

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.330
What's that smell?

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.630
Rin, let's go.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.800
-What?
-We just have to follow.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.560
Rin, let's go home and prepare.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.350
Prepare for what?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.320
Prepare to infiltrate.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.820
Hold on a second.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:19.240
If we believe what that map of yours says,

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.620
-then that hole leads to Edo Castle.
-And?

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.000
If they're doing experiments,
security won't be light.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.250
There's no way
the two of us can go in there alone.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:32.380
-We won't know until we try.
-But I do know.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.760
And how do you expect to do this
with just a map and our swords?

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.340
That may be the case,

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.590
-but...
-What is it?

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.650
Are you sure it was okay to take these?

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:56.900
It's fine, it's fine.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.360
Rin, what's that?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:16.300
Yes. More. I'll narrow it down even more.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:20.630
Like sifting through mud to find gold.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.140
Who is it from?

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:32.770
From Mr. Ayame, sir.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.700
SUCCESS

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.540
I imagine you'll be going to where Mr. Manji is.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.000
Yes.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.670
So of course, you're here
to get me involved, right?

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.050
So you're telling me,

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:04.680
you're going in with a plan
that amounts to a gamble?

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.220
This is a woman's fight.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:11.020
At times like these,
a woman's intuition is never wrong.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.350
A woman's intuition, huh?

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.570
I'm sorry.

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:19.530
I heard the story from Mr. Giichi.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:23.320
Either way, you're the only person I can turn to.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:26.740
Don't be silly. I'm glad.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.200
Thank you for telling me.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.410
Still, that guy...

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.210
When did you notice?

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.340
When you arrived here.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:46.800
So you're telling me I should stay quiet.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.140
That's right.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.810
If you have the experience, take good care of it.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.270
Take good care of it?

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.270
You think I'll birth this child?

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.190
The child bears no sin.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.620
Hey, Giichi. You're pretty nosy, you know?

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:13.250
And there's something off about it, all of it.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:25.470
Let go!

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.060
I...

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:38.060
I'm no good.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.900
Every time I see the child's face,

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.780
I'll remember it all.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.610
The child doesn't deserve that.

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:47.280
I'll raise it.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.950
Yes, I certainly am nosy.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:55.910
But a life devoted only to oneself is useless.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:13:59.330
Hyaku.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:04.090
Would you ever be able to face your dead child
after having killed one?

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:11.890
Giichi.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.520
Today, I'm going to kill people.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:22.730
Our master says it's okay to kill
in order to protect people you love.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.070
So I'll get rid of everyone in the way.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.490
Fine by me.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.450
To tell the truth,

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:33.080
I do value Mr. Manji's life a bit more
than some random stranger's.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.830
Get back! Get back!

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:38.710
Just where do you people think you are?

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.420
Hey, Mr. Samurai!

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.460
Please give me back my husband!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.880
-What the--?
-What is it?

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.970
What's happened to my husband?

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:56.810
You think we would know anything
about your husbands?

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.390
What are you doing?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.770
Just kill two or three of them to shut them up.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:01.690
Right.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.730
Please wait a moment, good sir.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:11.030
You've drawn your sword,
but it won't find a suitable opponent here.

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.580
Isn't this just what women do?

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:26.590
Send my husband home!

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.670
Let us see them!

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.680
Mr. Samurai, my husband.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.890
How many of you do I have to tell?

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:42.310
Give me a break.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.990
Get their husbands out too,

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.200
Rin.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.040
You killed six people

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.880
and knocked out two?

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.550
That's unbelievable.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:08.590
Though,

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.840
if that's true, the two of you are criminals.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.260
Let's see.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.680
Shall we start with whipping?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.970
Fifty lashes each.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.310
Fifty?

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.180
Isn't that a bit much?

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.270
They're just girls.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.650
And normally, we'd hand them over.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:27.570
That's just the rule on the surface.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:31.110
We're in the darkness,
where no one's eyes can see us.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.360
-If you get it, begin the preparations.
-Wait!

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.660
The lashes.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.660
I will take them all myself.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.120
-What?
-But you'll...

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.170
Now, why would you do that?

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:45.920
I only hired this girl

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.800
to carry my belongings,
since she has good night vision.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.800
She hasn't committed a crime worthy of a whipping.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:58.850
Promise me,

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:01.220
that if I endure this whipping,

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.850
our debts are paid.

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:06.020
I'll make that promise,

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:09.480
but that's assuming you're still
alive after 100 of them.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:12.690
Rin!

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.110
You... I'll kill all you idiots!

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:17.240
One.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:19.580
Two.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.000
Lord Sakura,

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:24.790
if you swing that hard, by the 100th, she'll be...

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.500
Don't you worry about it.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.300
Rin! Rin! You jerks!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.660
Why did you do that?

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.540
What? Oh, well,

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.580
if I let you get hurt,
then this was all for nothing.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:10.500
Don't look so sad.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:12.380
I'm prepared for this kind of thing.

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:19.640
The place we just left has a sun cross symbol on it.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.100
I thought this sign denoted a passageway,

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:26.100
but there are lots of these marks
around the center.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.850
You think someone would break in now?

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.270
-Thieves!
-Stop them!

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.860
Hold it!

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.240
Rin!

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:45.790
Hurry!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.380
Go on ahead.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.670
Hey, leave the spears.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.660
What was that?

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:22.910
Sir,

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:28.120
I just heard through the chain of command
that intruders are inside the castle.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.080
Surely, they can't be...

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:34.250
What was that noise?

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.690
Rin! Where are you?

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.650
Doa, I'm right here.

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.780
Sorry, but could you lend a hand?

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:08.830
I think my shoulder is dislocated.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:12.710
You're lucky it was just your shoulder.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.180
Don't space out like that!

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.560
Right, sorry.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:35.690
Doa!

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:39.320
What? You...

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:42.780
-Wait!
-Why are you stopping me?

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:43.780
Look.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:51.960
If they're all like that,
we don't have time to fight them.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
Escaping would be much quicker.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.040
Trust me.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.230
What is this?

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:51.930
Rin.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.980
Go on ahead without me.

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:54.850
Act Sixteen – Altered Limb
